## 6. Run list (minimal, ordered)

Commonsense, LLaMA-2-7B:

| # | Run | Knob | Seeds | Purpose |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | base (no adapter) eval | — | — | gate 1 |
| 1 | LoRA | — | 3 | gate 2 + baseline point |
| 2 | CLoRA-random | k ∈ {128, 256, 512, 1024, 2048} | 3 on k2048, 1 elsewhere | gate 3 + anchor curve |
| 3 | UIOrthoLoRA | (k_val,k_vec) × 4–5 | 3 on best, 1 elsewhere | the test |
| 3b | UILinLoRA (k_vec=0) | — | 1 | curve endpoint / ablation |

≈ 13–15 commonsense runs. **If GO**, immediately add the math follow-on:

Math, LLaMA-2-7B (rank 64, α 128, MetaMathQA 395K, GSM8K+MATH EM):

| # | Run | Knob |
|---|---|---|
| 4 | LoRA | — |
| 5 | CLoRA-random | k ∈ {64, 128, 256} |
| 6 | UIOrthoLoRA | (k_val,k_vec) × 3 |

Math targets to confirm anchor: LoRA GSM8K 60.58/MATH 16.88; CLoRA-k128 64.59/18.38 (best — note CLoRA *degrades* past k=128 on math; this capacity ceiling is exactly the seam UIOrthoLoRA's medium tier may exploit).

